cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use espmap, please cite it as below, and also cite the methods and
  software it builds on: PySCF, RDKit, and the electrostatic-potential and
  molecular-surface literature listed in docs/prior-art.md, with full
  entries in docs/references.bib.
type: software
title: "espmap: electrostatic-potential maps for organic molecules"
abstract: >-
  DFT electrostatic potential evaluated at the vertices of the
  rho = 0.002 e/bohr^3 density isosurface, with a structure gate, surface
  integrity checks, a measured error budget and a colour scale chosen from
  the data. Research code.
authors:
  - family-names: Wongsatit
    given-names: Thanakrit
    alias: Austin
version: 0.3.1
date-released: 2026-10-25
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Azuromalachite/espmap"
keywords:
  - chemistry
  - electrostatic potential
  - DFT
  - molecular surface
  - sigma-hole
  - colormap
